{"id":"carbender","name":"Carbender","url":"https://devpost.com/software/carbender","summary":"A tool for identifying damaged car parts and estimating repair costs. Computer vision turns photos into organized OEM part lists with real-market price reports.","event":"Build with Gemini XPRIZE","event_org":"XPRIZE","event_date":"2026-08-17","domain":"Money, Commerce & Marketplaces","subsystem":"Retail & Conversion","moves":[],"stack":["antigravity","cloudflare-r2","gemini-api","google-genai","google-search-grounding","inngest","neon.tech","next.js","node.js","postgresql"],"likes":2,"award":"Unknown","coolness":0.4245,"coolness_parts":{"engagement":0.1404,"validation":0.1,"event_prestige":0.8196,"recency":0.9508,"specificity":0.62,"signal_richness":0.75,"redundancy":0.0938,"total":0.4245},"depth":"deep","has_deep":1,"repo_url":null,"demo_url":"https://carbender.com","video_url":"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=gXPxplOgSPY","provenance":{"likes":"observed","summary":"observed","built_with":"observed","domain":"derived","moves":"derived","stack":"derived","specificity":"derived","coolness":"derived","event":"observed","award":"unavailable"},"harvested_at":"2026-09-18","audit":{"verdict":"sound-with-caveats","worth":"niche","soundness":"partial","soundness_score":0.5703,"rubric_coverage":0.64,"checks":{"artifact_exists":"supported","build_is_real":"unverifiable","limits_disclosed":"confirmed","numbers_add_up":"partial","stack_consistency":"unverifiable","test_or_eval_evidence":"unverifiable"},"unknowns":[],"evidence":6,"hazard":{"class":"regulated-claim","note":"This is a money decision dressed in regulatory vocabulary. The product returns a Total Loss verdict and a repair estimate that a buyer may bid against, while invoking DOT, SAE and ECE standards, country-specific import, title, emissions and inspection requirements, and a Loss Ratio band policy described as 'matching EU & US salvage threshold standards' with no citation and no named issuing body for either threshold. Nothing on the page states who is liable when the estimate is wrong, no accuracy figure exists for either the part identification or the price, and the resale denominator comes from another estimate rather than a transaction record, so a High-band verdict near a boundary can flip on inputs that are both soft. The team's stated posture is the right instinct - a wrong OEM code shown with false confidence is worse than no result - but an interface banner is not a compliance sign-off, and a tool that names regulators should either cite them or stop invoking them. Held from promotion on that basis: publishable as a documented case, not as a usable figure.","team_disclaimed":false},"repo":null,"audited_at":"2026-09-19","audit_version":1,"sheet":"data/audits/money-commerce-and-marketplaces.json#carbender"}}
